  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Legal Aid - HIV/AIDS - Rio de Janeiro</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project with Grupo Pela Vidda &#x2013; Rio de Janeiro (GPV-RJ), seeks to protect and promote the social and individual rights of people living with HIV and AIDS, in Brazil. 

Areas of work include legal aid, counselling and support groups. Over the years, Grupo Pela Vidda has become a very politically active organization participating and promoting a wide range of activities from counselling and community care to high level advocacy through pressure on the government to take action against the epidemic and on discrimination against PLWHA.  GPV promotes the empowerment of people living with HIV and AIDS in Rio de Janeiro and in Brazil. 
This new three year plan represents a number of changes that GPV has been undergoing over the last few years. GPV will focus their next 3 year plan on consolidating their network of legal consultants, as well as trying to invest more in taking a more strategic approach to advocacy, involving PLWHA to ensure that they can gain the rights set out in the constitution and become protagonists in their own future.</narrative>
  </description>
